# Example ~/.arrangrr.init — copy to $HOME/.arrangrr.init to use it.
#
# The live TUI auto-runs ~/.arrangrr.init on every launch (no flag), after the
# panels open and ~/.arrangrr.rc is applied. It is a plain list of shell
# commands (the same grammar the REPL accepts). It is LENIENT: a bad line only
# warns to the console and startup continues — a stale default never bricks the
# TUI. An explicit `--init FILE` overrides the auto-load and is STRICT (a bad
# line aborts). Blank lines and '#' comments are ignored.
#
# This example configures the "single-finger live steering" session: you play
# one key and that key alone imposes the chord the whole band follows.
#
# GLOBAL CHORD STEERING (no pitch split): whenever ANY panel has focus (anything
# but the REPL command line), a musical NOTE-letter key steers the band SILENTLY
# — from the piano, chords, parts, groove, styles or arp panel alike. The
# note-key takes priority over that panel's own letter shortcuts. Detection is ON
# out of the box, so no `chord detect on` is needed. The live chord readout
# (playing / holding) lives in the CHORDS panel.

# Single-finger chords: one held key = the scale-aware maj/min triad (a second
# key colours it). This line is now REDUNDANT — configure_default_surfaces()
# already starts a fresh launch in single mode — but it is kept as documentation
# and to make an explicit session self-describing.
chord mode single

# Live-priority chord following (the engine default): your live keys always beat
# the chord sequencer while held — the band follows your finger and the sequencer
# (if one runs) comps on your chord; when you let go the sequencer resumes. With no
# sequencer a live chord simply latches. This line is REDUNDANT (kLivePriority is
# already the default) but keeps the session self-describing. Alternatives:
# `chord follow detect` (detect-only, the sequencer never steers) or
# `chord follow sequencer` (a recorded progression drives hands-free).
chord follow live

# Load a style so there is a band to hear. Swap for any builtin:
#   basic pop rock ballad funk disco house swing bossa samba
#   reggae country blues shuffle latin motown
style load basic

# The band is NOT started automatically — press CTRL+P to play/stop.
# To auto-start it on launch instead, uncomment the next line:
# transport start
